  "definition_ja": "定規や分度器などの道具を使って、長さや角の大きさなどを数で調べる。",
  "definition_en": "To find the size of something, such as a length or an angle, as a number of units, usually with a tool like a ruler or a protractor.",
  "latex": null,
  "spoken_en": null,
  "examples": [
    {
      "en": "Grab your protractor and measure angle B. You should get about 65 degrees.",
      "ja": "分度器を出して、角 B を測ってみて。だいたい 65° になるはず。",
      "register": "spoken"
    },
    {
      "en": "Use a ruler to measure the length of segment AB to the nearest tenth of a centimeter.",
      "ja": "定規を使って、線分 AB の長さを 0.1 cm 単位で測れ。",
      "register": "written"
    }
  ],
  "collocations": [],
  "pitfalls": [
    "名詞の measure は「大きさ」の意味で使う。∠A の大きさは the measure of angle A で、m∠A と書く（m∠A = 50°）。",
    "道具は、長さなら ruler（定規・ものさし）、角なら protractor（分度器）。measure … with a ruler ／ with a protractor の形で言う。",
    "統計の measure of central tendency（代表値。エントリ measure-of-center）の measure は「指標」の意味で、「測る」とは別。"
  ],
